 <=5 times 1 MiB median. Serialized sizes and all samples are reported separately.
 These are implementation acceptance budgets, never body-size limits. Results do
 not qualify another host or authorize deployment; independent verification follows.
+
+
+## Experimental transcript view — conditional publication candidate
+
+This candidate adds a separate transcript reader behind the same source-only
+signpost and keyboard. Permanent processor placement under Nablarva L8/L8′,
+final qualification and reviewed publication/activation remain pending. It is
+not enabled by a host startup file or a service. Composition behavior and its
+request grammar remain independent.
+
+After explicitly sourcing this directory's `base.zsh`, `tbv-render`, `tbv-select`,
+`tbv-pin`, `tbv-open`, `tbv-collect`, `tbv-status`, `tbv-refresh` and `tbv-watch`
+call the adjacent stdlib Python helpers. For noninteractive use, invoke the
+corresponding `_tbv_*` function after source, as for the composer examples above.
+`transcript.py --help` and `collector.py --help` describe their explicit inputs.
+Sourcing starts no Python, scan, collector, editor or native session. `open` is an
+explicit editor action; `watch` is an explicitly started bounded foreground poll.
+
+The default `synthetic-event-jsonl` format is a fictional fixture contract, not
+native history support. Explicit `codex-rollout-0.166` and `codex-rollout-0.167`
+formats read separately versioned, source-derived text subsets; the 0.167 subset
+reads completed message items and checks producer-version metadata. A single
+explicit disposable Codex 0.167 capture has been parsed; complete history,
+inherited branches, compaction reconstruction and live approval answerability
+are not qualified. Claude JSONL remains an unqualified synthetic
+fixture adapter. There is no native session discovery, resume, input injection
+or approval forwarding. Historical approval evidence cannot establish a current
+pending decision; unavailable outcomes remain unknown.
+
+Snapshots retain a complete captured prefix, deterministic Markdown and mapping.
+Bookmarks bind to an immutable snapshot; validated exact-prefix continuity is
+required for carry-forward. Observable replacement, shortening or mutation
+blocks carry-forward. An unobserved same-inode rewrite restoring identical bytes
+cannot be distinguished from append. Collection leaves the selected reading
+stable until explicit refresh. A crash between selected-pointer and derived-copy
+writes is detected by implicit engine readers and repaired by collector
+status/collect/refresh; these are not atomic multi-file writes. An already-open
+file may still display its earlier captured content until explicitly reopened.
+
+The task-scoped `~/.nablarva/<project>/<bed>/cache.<session>` and
+`read.<session>.md` layout is an experimental operator exception; it is not a
+standing configuration decision. Snapshots can be the last retained source
+behind bookmarks. No automatic eviction or reboot cleanup is implemented.
+
+Transcript fixtures and checks are separate from composer tests:
+
+```sh
+python3 -I -S -B -m unittest discover -s transcript-tests -v
+```
+
+The Sublime observation connector is separate development tooling and is not
+included in this publication candidate. Programmatic path/text/caret checks do
+not prove visual rendering, native history fidelity or operator usability.
